ke  just in terms of representation like  just  yeah the different faces we're finally  getting to see in marvel like  what does it feel like to be part of  that new wave for new face  i mean yeah it's it's it's amazing and  it and it's  incredible and you know um even  know yeah like latinas are a little bit  like missing kind of sort of  in terms of characters so to um  to be originating one you know and our  show is sort of  separate from like the film emcee  film world um so which is good because  it kind of allows us to have a little  bit more  fun with you know like we have iron man  makes an appearance in our show and  uh so but it's so  and to see what it means to all people  of color you know it's  i mean we remember what it felt like  when black panther came out  and just it's meaningful  it's when you see a superhero that looks  like you  and the subconscious implications that  that can have  is everything um so  i'm thrilled to be like a tiny speck of  that  that moved that movement forward and i'm  really excited to see  the films that are going to be coming  out and um it's just an exciting time  yeah is your five year old still as  obsessed with avengers  and marvel as he is he is  a brand new miles morales costume just  so nice in the mail today that he wanted  to wear to school and they said no you  can't wear that to preschool  and uh yeah jordan um our show runner  from modoc  very sweetly put together this amazing  starter pack of comics for my son um  and so we just started diving into some  of that um  so there's a lot of like great  spider-man issues he gave us and  some avenger ones and so it's amazing  yeah it's really fun  yeah so i love your character like wants  to become a super villain  and what i find so interesting about  like this new wave of marvel that we've  had over the past few months  like comedians like yourself are really  getting into  the marvel world like you and patton in  this show juliud louis dreyfus is  playing a villain that we get just got  introduced  and then even like catherine hahn on one  division so what do you make of like  like like like big comedians like  yourself obviously there's been  comic actors before but real true  comedians are now getting into  the marvel world i love it i love to  keep it i love it  um it's so exciting and you know  i think it makes sense too because  there's something kind of  that can be you know comedy can be  really theatrical and i think you have  to have that sensibility  um to play big characters like  superheroes um so you know when you  think of it that way like that  it doesn't feel like that big of a leap  um you know  our show i would say is  very much a comedy so  you know i i can't really like toot my  own horn that much because i'm just like  doing what they expected me to do and  funny  you know i'm not i'm definitely not  pulling off what catherine hahn did  in one division she was so incredible um  and i loved her performance so much and  it was so smart of them to  cast her in that role because that was a  really tough duality that she had to  play  um and i thought she nailed it so it was  thrilling to watch but but there's a lot  of comedy in the pa  in in the comics too you know right a  lot of  that exists in the world so um yeah i  love it  were you shocked at the i'm trying to  think the right word let me if crass  this is the right word but like the  the yes the little non-pg  side of modoc of the yeah were you  surprised at that  i mean yes and no because it was patent  and so  i was like oh this makes sense  you know if you know him or his comedy  and you know if you watch any of us  stand up like um  you know patent's a little filthy  [Laughter]  so but i i loved it because it really  in that sense it felt so different and  so fresh  and you know we've been living with the  superheroes for  a while now and a lot of different  iterations of them  so to me it was really fun  to see a version of this world that was